      },
      {
        "body": "Keep the workspace flat, using the existing line and field surfaces to express structure.",
        "name": "The Shared Ground Rule",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Plum brand and action on a lavender ground.",
      "Humanist type with clear, weighted labels.",
      "Flat regions separated by thin lines.",
      "Explicit empty, loading, error, and saved states."
    ],
    "overview": "A quiet, practical workspace uses humanist type, a plum identity, and a pale lavender ground. The visual character comes from typography and the relationship between entry and result, with little ornament and no raised card layer.\n\nThe current surface is an English anonymous URL creation utility. Its amber notice communicates the actual availability limitation before entry; the result area represents saved data only. Future surfaces should preserve this clarity without treating this page's particular composition as a universal template."
  }
